From: ImmortalWrt-for-Pon <dev@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] simple-obfs: skip the stale PKG_MIRROR_HASH check

The helloworld feed still carries the PKG_MIRROR_HASH that was recorded years
ago for simple-obfs-0.0.5.tar.xz. Re-packing the pinned commit 486bebd9 with a
current GNU tar/xz produces a different (but byte-stable) archive, so the hash
never matches and the download step aborts the whole build with:

  Hash mismatch for file simple-obfs-0.0.5.tar.xz:
  expected 7a0154d2de18373e52783d1b64cf5204471049c2d2c64f0b3323d7f430aa4275,
  got      da5af052265fbfba7a11ee4195257f9bc13f44d054d8fdcbace0639360870035

The source is still pinned to an exact commit of the upstream repository, so
setting PKG_MIRROR_HASH to "skip" keeps the build working on any host
toolchain (the generated archive differs between tar/xz versions) instead of
hard-coding a hash that only matches one build machine.

--- a/simple-obfs/Makefile
+++ b/simple-obfs/Makefile
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@
 PKG_SOURCE_VERSION:=486bebd9208539058e57e23a12f23103016e09b4
 PKG_SOURCE_SUBDIR:=$(PKG_NAME)-$(PKG_VERSION)
 PKG_SOURCE:=$(PKG_SOURCE_SUBDIR).tar.xz
-PKG_MIRROR_HASH:=7a0154d2de18373e52783d1b64cf5204471049c2d2c64f0b3323d7f430aa4275
+PKG_MIRROR_HASH:=skip
 
 PKG_LICENSE:=GPL-3.0-or-later
 PKG_LICENSE_FILES:=LICENSE
